NEARS-1321 — Store-origin chip MISSING on live Buy It Again card
Device: emulator-5554 | Build: fresh worktree app-debug.apk (Gradle assembleDebug + Installing verified) | User: customer@nears.com (id 6, "Customer Nears") | Zone 1 | Grocery module (id 1)

EVIDENCE CHAIN (chip should render, but does not):

1. BACKEND API returns store_name (verified via curl, app-identical headers):
   GET /api/v1/customer/order/buy-it-again  (zoneId:[1] moduleId:1)
   -> total_size 1
   -> product id 99 | name "Mango" | store_id 1 | store_name = "Nears Mart"   (NON-NULL)

2. FLUTTER code path is correct (static review):
   - item_that_you_love_view.dart:182  ItemWidget(... showStoreOrigin: true)  (BIA rail, forShop:false)
   - item_widget.dart:144  showStoreBadge = showStoreOrigin && storeName != null && storeName.trim().isNotEmpty
   - item_widget.dart:205-216  renders NearsBadge(info, Symbols.storefront, item.storeName)
   - item_model.dart:206  storeName = json['store_name']
   - ItemModel.fromJson -> Item.fromJson maps products (item_model.dart:20-23)
   - Widget test test/common/widgets/item_widget_store_origin_test.dart: 7/7 PASS (chip renders when storeName set)

3. LIVE (fresh build): chip is ABSENT on the only BIA card.
   uiautomator dump, Mango card node bounds [45,1479][540,2298]:
     content-desc="10% OFF\nMango\nkg\nNEW\n21 AED\n23 AED"
   -> discount badge "10% OFF" IS present in the merged a11y tree
   -> NO store-name node ("NEARS MART" / "Nears Mart") anywhere within the card bounds
   -> Screenshot bug-store-origin-chip-missing-on-bia.png: only the red "10% OFF" pill + favourite heart; the image area below the discount badge is empty (no store chip)

4. Logs-first: NO [ERR]/[FAIL]/render exception during BIA render (not a swallowed-error case).

CONCLUSION: the store NearsBadge widget is NOT in the tree (its Text would appear in a11y like the discount Text does) => showStoreBadge=false at runtime => item.storeName is null/blank at the widget at runtime, EVEN THOUGH the API returns store_name="Nears Mart" and Item.fromJson maps it. The gap is in the buy-it-again data->widget integration (Item deserialization / list the widget reads), NOT in the chip widget code (widget + unit test are correct).

NOTE: exact runtime value of item.storeName could not be captured — the Dart VM service / DDS was unstable on this shared emulator (flutter run repeatedly "Lost connection to device"; VM /ws 302-redirected to a dead DDS; only trivial getVersion responded over HTTP). Root cause above is INFERRED from the a11y tree + correct widget code + valid API data. Recommend the engineer add a temporary AppLogger on the BIA parse (or a hot-reload inspection) to confirm item.storeName at the widget.
